// GET https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/documents.rss (first two items, one category each)
FEDERAL_REGISTER_RSS """
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">
  <channel>
    <title>Federal Register Documents published on or after 10/05/2026</title>
    <link>https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/documents.rss</link>
    <pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 05:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
    <description>The documents in this feed originate from FederalRegister.gov which displays an unofficial web version of the daily Federal Register. The official electronic version in PDF format is also available as a link from the FederalRegister.gov website. For more information, please see https://www.federalregister.gov/reader-aids/policy/legal-status.</description>
<item>
      <title>Treatment of Emergency Amendments: Paycheck Protection Program Liquidity Facility and Paycheck Protection Program Loans</title>
      <link>https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/11/04/2026-22538/treatment-of-emergency-amendments-paycheck-protection-program-liquidity-facility-and-paycheck</link>
      <description>The NCUA Board (Board) is issuing a final rule adopting as final the revisions to the capital adequacy rule and the member business lending rule made under an interim final rule (IFR) published in the Federal Register on April 27, 2020.</description>
      <pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 05:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/11/04/2026-22538/treatment-of-emergency-amendments-paycheck-protection-program-liquidity-facility-and-paycheck</guid>
      <dc:creator>National Credit Union Administration</dc:creator>
      <category>Banks, banking</category>
</item>
<item>
      <title>Member Business Loans; Commercial Lending</title>
      <link>https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/11/04/2026-22537/member-business-loans-commercial-lending</link>
      <description>The NCUA Board (Board) is amending its regulations governing member business loans and commercial lending. This interim final rule eliminates an outdated, transitional provision that is no longer necessary. This action is necessary to reduce regulatory complexity and improve the clarity of the NCUA&amp;#39;s regulations. The intended effect is to enhance clarity and simplify compliance for federally insured credit unions (FICUs).</description>
      <pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 05:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/11/04/2026-22537/member-business-loans-commercial-lending</guid>
      <dc:creator>National Credit Union Administration</dc:creator>
      <category>Credit</category>
</item>
  </channel>
</rss>
"""

